Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["8) CLM conventions and quadratic comparison", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"7e89188f-5951-47dc-9d57-68b31db01cdf"],

Cell["\<\
Our action convention is S = kappa^(-2) integral h^{mu nu} R_{mu nu}, before \
the optional overall factor 1/2 discussed after Eq. (5.1). CLM uses 2 K^(-2) \
integral h^{mu nu} R^CLM_{mu nu} in Eq. (2.1), with the opposite Ricci sign \
in Eq. (2.2). Identifying K = kappa and the same metric-density perturbation \
therefore gives L3 = -(kappa/2) L_(3)^CLM. This is an action/curvature \
convention difference, not a Fourier i^2 factor. At quadratic order the \
corresponding relation is L2 + L_(2)^CLM/2 = CD_a J^a. CLM factors the \
coupling as L = Sum[K^(j-2) L_(j), j >= 2], so lag2CLM and lag3CLM are the \
coefficients without their coupling powers.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ed02daf0-925b-47d2-ba8e-bfdd969da90d"],

Cell["\<\
Eliminating G gives L2 = -(1/2) partial(phi) M0Inverse partial(phi). The \
following cells construct this quadratic Lagrangian and compare it with CLM \
before proceeding to cubic order.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2041ddea-b633-40b0-a135-d441abdb7124"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"lag2", "=", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"ToCanonical", "[", 
     RowBox[{"ContractMetric", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"-", "1"}], "/", "2"}], " ", "g0Up", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"CD", "[", 
         RowBox[{"-", "a"}], "]"}], "[", 
        RowBox[{"phi", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"-", "b"}], ",", 
          RowBox[{"-", "c"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], "//", 
    "Simplify"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.998395258137678*^9, 3.9983952679583797`*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[52]:=",ExpressionUUID->"2e43b779-e994-45af-b456-2a0f26791c5a"],

